 "best_idea": "A zone spawn rate as a per-zone-kind 1-in-N roll on each clock step, inside a fixed 12-of-144 window, gated by presence (outdoor, dungeon while resting and alerted), with a server-side rule and no per-frame randomness.",
 "decision": "adapt",
 "decision_why": "The window shape and per-zone odds fit zones as data, but the donor has no population cap and its per-frame catch-up drops rolls after a spawn, so we take the window and odds and rebuild the cap and the step on the fixed server tick.",
 "decision_status": "proposed",
 "acceptance": "Server test with a seeded RNG and a night rule of 1 in 24: advance a zone clock 1440 steps one minute at a time; every spawn falls inside a 12-minute window of a 144-minute period, no two spawns share a minute, and the live spawn count never exceeds the zone cap (row 23)."
